    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "193b52ec_499461a3",
        "filename": "common/acpi.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 191,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-05T00:51:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It needs *a* cast here to get a byte-addressible pointer since we\u0027re starting with a `struct battery_static_info*`, but after studying what C11 has to say about pointer casts, arithmetic and UB I do think we\u0027re okay to skip the intermediate `uintptr_t`.",
      "parentUuid": "02f05caf_85bda9ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "17d752aa7efdb4f7bdad5c1638bf2fd9626e02a9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f077f87_b4921c65",
        "filename": "common/acpi.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 203,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-04T14:35:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, the 2nd time EC_ACPI_MEM_STRINGS_FIFO_ID_VERSION is read, we return 0 (because strings_fifo_offset will be incremented on the 1st read). Isn\u0027t it confusing from the AP\u0027s perspective?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 203,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "17d752aa7efdb4f7bdad5c1638bf2fd9626e02a9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eca5cda8_5b0d9a29",
        "filename": "common/acpi.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 203,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-05T00:51:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Perhaps, but I opted to give this index the same behavior as the others (continuously reading zero after reaching the end of the data) since that also simplifies possible extensions to this field later (if it turns out to want to be able to return more than one byte).",
      "parentUuid": "8f077f87_b4921c65",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 203,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "17d752aa7efdb4f7bdad5c1638bf2fd9626e02a9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb78d088_7c88e722",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 557,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-04T14:35:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, this controls how the strings are read. Shall we give it a dedicated field (new acpi address) so that the AP can query it independently?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 556,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 557,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "17d752aa7efdb4f7bdad5c1638bf2fd9626e02a9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "611d2ab8_2211cb5a",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 557,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-05T00:51:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there\u0027s any reason to. The EC always returns 0xff for reads of unknown addresses and ignores writes to them, so the AP can always safely probe for support by writing 0 here and checking that it reads back a value that is not zero (perhaps an EC that understands this feature but has it disabled) and not 0xff (an EC that doesn\u0027t understand this feature).",
      "parentUuid": "bb78d088_7c88e722",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 556,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 557,
        "endChar": 37
      },
